I want to build a simple web tool to take user inputs (initial velocity, release height, launch angle, and distance from the hoop) to determine whether a basketball shot will go in/ through the rim. What are three common outputs i can have this program spit out and what are some simple features i can add.
Your basketball shot calculator is a great idea for a CS1 project because it has a clear input → processing → output structure. You can use basic Python math to calculate the ball's trajectory and determine whether it would pass through the hoop.
I would recommend three main outputs and a few simple features that make the application more interesting without making it too complicated.
1. Three common outputs
1. Shot Result (Make or Miss)
MAKE
Shot goes in!
The ball passes through the rim.
MISS
Shot misses!
The ball misses the rim.
The program determines whether the basketball's trajectory passes through the hoop.
This should be your primary output.
You can display a large MAKE or MISS message.
2. Maximum Shot Height
Display how high the basketball travels before it starts falling back down.
For example:
Maximum height: 14.2 feet
Maximum height: 18.6 feet
Maximum height: 21.3 feet
This would help users understand how much arc their shot has.
3. Ball Height When It Reaches the Hoop
Calculate the height of the basketball when it reaches the horizontal distance of the hoop.
For example:
Hoop height: 10 feet
Ball height at hoop: 10.4 feet
Difference: +0.4 feet
This helps explain WHY a shot goes in or misses.
Important: For a realistic make/miss calculation, you should also account for the basketball's radius and the rim's radius. For a simplified CS1 project, you can initially treat the ball as a point and use a simplified hoop-crossing check.
